WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.525
Calibration means matching confidence to actual knowledge, skill, accuracy, or likelihood.

2
00:00:04.525 --> 00:00:07.815
Good calibration does not mean always being uncertain.

3
00:00:07.815 --> 00:00:11.106
It means confidence rises and falls with evidence.

4
00:00:11.106 --> 00:00:16.453
If you are highly confident, you should be able to point to why.

5
00:00:16.453 --> 00:00:20.155
If evidence is weak, confidence should be more cautious.

6
00:00:20.155 --> 00:00:25.502
Calibration helps people decide when to act, check, learn, or ask for help.

7
00:00:25.502 --> 00:00:29.615
Overconfidence is risky because it can stop checking too early.

8
00:00:29.615 --> 00:00:35.785
A person may skip testing, ignore feedback, or dismiss uncertainty because the answer feels obvious.

9
00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:37.842
Underconfidence is also a problem.

10
00:00:37.842 --> 00:00:44.012
It can prevent people from using real capability, taking appropriate action, or accepting useful challenge.

11
00:00:44.012 --> 00:00:50.182
Both problems distort performance because confidence no longer matches what the person can actually do.

12
00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:53.061
Prediction checks are a simple calibration tool.

13
00:00:53.061 --> 00:01:00.876
Estimate how likely an answer is, how well you understand a topic, or how successful an approach will be.

14
00:01:00.876 --> 00:01:03.755
Then compare the estimate with the result.

15
00:01:03.755 --> 00:01:05.812
Confidence ratings can also help.

16
00:01:05.812 --> 00:01:11.982
Before submitting an answer or making a decision, rate your confidence and note the evidence.

17
00:01:11.982 --> 00:01:15.684
Over time, you can see whether confidence is reliable.

18
00:01:15.684 --> 00:01:19.797
Feedback loops improve calibration when they are specific and timely.

19
00:01:19.797 --> 00:01:23.088
The point is not to punish being wrong.

20
00:01:23.088 --> 00:01:26.790
The point is to update beliefs based on evidence.

21
00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:38.307
Accurate self-assessment improves learning and decision quality because it helps you choose the right next action: continue, review, practice, test, slow down, or bring in another perspective.
